{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1541926-behold-i-give-you-the-d20-exalted-it-is-the-lightning-it-is-the-madness","id":1541926,"title":"Behold, I give you the d20 Exalted: It is the lightning, it is the madness.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-11T09:54:31-07:00","id":1541926,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Behold, I give you the d20 Exalted: It is the lightning, it is the madness.","content":"<span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Disclaimer: That's d20 as in &quot;based on twenty-sided dice,&quot; not d20 as in &quot;basically D&amp;D.&quot;</i></span><br /> <br /> I really like Exalted, as a setting and as a style. I'd love to run and play more Exalted games, but alas, the system (regardless of edition) tends be an unintuitive, clunky mess. I ran one two-year Exalted 3e campaign with a group of just three players--experienced players, people I've been gaming with for more than a decade more--and it was... memorable. There were awesome moments, and there were moments of sheer befuddled pain, moments when we hit upon awesome mechanics and moments where we screamed at the book for having subsystems that fall apart the moment you poke them. By the time we wrapped things up, the players had advanced to the point that combat encounters were complicated multi-stage (and usually multi-week) affairs, and my brain was well and truly broken.<br /> <br /> (I'm not sure it's ever recovered, to tell the truth).<br /> <br /> You can mostly use Mutants and Masterminds to run Exalted-style game, but you kind of needed to have a good grip on both Exalted themes and M&amp;M's initially-impenetrable power creation system. What I really wanted was to run a game for my in-person group, but they'd been confused enough last time we tried M&amp;M for superheroes. Trying to have them create their own characters that actually fit a setting they've never seen before... no, thanks.<br /> <br /> What I really needed, I decided, was some sort of unholy fusion of Exalted, M&amp;M, and 5e. Something with all the flavor and madness of Exalted, the familiarity and approachability of 5e, and the robust balancing and ease-of-play of M&amp;M.<br /> <br /> What I got was way too much free time. and a fresh new prescription for ADHD meds.<br /> <br /> What you get is this: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/18BOGw5A3RYsj-sj_pt1tzlUZ7mRPdK-H/view?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/18BO...w?usp=drivesdk</a> <hr /><br /> Practically speaking, there were three facets to the project.<br /> <br /> First, I had to make M&amp;M more approachable to people who've only played 5e. Updated action economy, simplified character creation, streamlined math, and so on. The most central of which was probably the creation of a three-tiered proficiency system: low, medium, and high bonuses that were slipped in anywhere M&amp;M would normally have a tradeoff. A medium weapon adds your medium bonus to attack and damage, for example, while a heavy weapon adds your minor to attack and major to damage. If you want a high Dodge save, one of your other saves is going to have to use the low bonus.<br /> <br /> Second, I had to expanded my D&amp;Dified-M&amp;M mess to include key features of Exalted--social conflict, anima, crafting, leadership, all that jazz.<br /> <br /> Third, and most insanely, charms. For each one, I took the Exalted flavor and mechanics and hammered it into M&amp;M's effects-and-modifiers system until it either fit of shattered completely. From there, I sorted them into tiers of power based on their M&amp;M costs--then shuffled them around again when the quirks of a superhero system left high-tier effects like Soul Projection Technique and Sometimes Horses Fly Approach dirt cheap. Finally, I pulled back and wrote out the effects in natural language as if they were 5e spells or class features, smoothing out awkward mechanical bumps and cracks in the process. Then I repeated the process until my eyes bled and I had almost 500 charms, spells, and evocations. <hr /><br /> At this point, I've run two campaigns with the system, and it's on what (despite the file name) is essentially its third edition. Not only does it play beautifully, even for my not-too-mechanically-savvy players, but now supports all six major Exalt types--Solar, Lunar, Sidereal, Dragon Blooded, Infernal, and Abyssal--with no homebrew needed! Specifically, as of 9/11/24,<ul><li>All rules necessary to create, play, and progress characters. (The rules are <i>done</i>, I'm just grinding my way through the charm lists.)</li> <li>Over a hundred merits to represent mortal skills and abilities.</li> <li>Almost three hundred universal skill- and combat-style-based charms available for all Exalt types.</li> <li>More than two dozen generic &quot;Supernatural Charms&quot; to cover a wide variety of non-Exalt creatures.</li> <li>Solars and Dragon Blooded are feature-complete, with their exalt/caste specific abilities in place and their ~60-charm unique charmsets fully written out.</li> <li>Lunars, Sidereals, Infernals, and Abyssals have their exalt/caste specific stuff finished, but their unique charmsets are currently limited to short descriptions. (Although there are more concrete charm creation guidelines than any edition of Exalted proper I've seen)</li> <li>Seven martial arts: Black Claw, Crane, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, Ebon Shadow, Silver-Voiced Nightingale, Snake, and White Reaper.</li> <li>Sorcery is complete; Necromancy is currently limited to a single Initiation and Shadowlands Circle spells. (Higher level spell lists exist but are currently limited to short descriptions.)</li> <li>Social Influence, imported practically word-for-word from Exalted 3e.</li> <li>Rules for running large-scale organizations like kingdoms and guilds.</li> <li>Warstriders!</li> <li>Guidelines for charm, encounter, and NPC design.</li> </ul><hr /><br /> Anyway. I've sunk a lot of blood, sweat, and tears into this. I hope ya'll find it interesting, at least.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Full disclosure: There are going to be typos, inconsistencies, and editing mistakes. I've tried, but this is a 400 page document with an extended development time and I'm just one lunatic. Also, apologies if you've already seen this posted in other places)</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T20:36:21-07:00","id":1542016,"title":"","content":"Is this also compatible with 3.5e based d20?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T04:46:01-07:00","id":1542041,"title":"","content":"Not even a little bit. Ex20 is primarily based on Mutants and Masterminds 3e, which shares a bunch of terminology and action economy stuff with d&amp;d but is very much it's own beast. <br /> <br /> If you're looking for Exalted-esque 3.5 material, Xefas' Mythos classes are pretty cool. <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?517754-Mythos-Compendium-2-0\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.giantitp.com/showthre...Compendium-2-0</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T17:59:04-07:00","id":1542518,"title":"","content":"Now announcing the &quot;Martial Arts Update&quot;-- an across-the-board overhaul of martial arts access and charm progression systems and a whopping eleven new styles: Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, Tiger, Righteous Devil, Single Point, Steel Devil, all five Elemental Dragon styles, and Prismatic Arrangement of Creation. Check it out!<br /> <br /> (The link in the OP should still work, as should this one: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=18BOGw5A3RYsj-sj_pt1tzlUZ7mRPdK-H&amp;usp=drive_fs\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=18B...H&amp;usp=drive_fs</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T08:58:31-07:00","id":1542551,"title":"","content":"How long did this take you?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T06:11:40-07:00","id":1542623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1541926-behold-i-give-you-the-d20-exalted-it-is-the-lightning-it-is-the-madness?p=1542551#post1542551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long did this take you?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#2980b9\">I prefer not to answer on the grounds that it may incriminate me.</span><br /> <br /> (On and off for three years, as hyperfixations waxed and waned)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T17:35:25-07:00","id":1544242,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Now announcing the &quot;Iconic Update,&quot; with a selection of representative charms for the as-yet-unfinished Exalt varieties. I picked what I felt were the most iconic castes for each Exalt type I've yet to finish-- Casteless Lunars (ie, &quot;all shapeshifting stuff&quot;), Secrets Sidereals, Daybreak Abyssals, and Ascendant Infernals--and written up their unique charms. I figure that if the caste is reasonably representative of the whole, their charm list can sort of extend to cover the other castes in a pinch. Take a look!<br /> <br /> The original link should still work, as should this one: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=18BOGw5A3RYsj-sj_pt1tzlUZ7mRPdK-H&amp;usp=drive_fs\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=18B...H&amp;usp=drive_fs</a></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}